   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I would like to make a panel conditional on a file being uploaded.</div><div><br></div><div>One way I think I can do that is to take inspiration from the example shown in <a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#uploads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/%23uploads&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407464953000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1e1j4ysyA9MkJJ9KVbNv5v\">http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#uploads</a></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:9px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902)\"><code style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;color:inherit;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\">    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># input$file1 will be NULL initially. After the user selects and uploads a </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># file, it will be a data frame with &#39;name&#39;, &#39;size&#39;, &#39;type&#39;, and &#39;datapath&#39; </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># columns. The &#39;datapath&#39; column will contain the local filenames where the </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># data can be found.</span></span>\r\n\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inFile</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">file1</span>\r\n\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">if</span></span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">is.null</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inFile</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span>\r\n      <span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">return</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(88,72,246)\">NULL</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I am wondering what is the right way to compose this condition:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:9px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902)\"><code style=\"color:inherit;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">conditionalPanel</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span>\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">condition</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;input.file1 != null&quot;</span>,\r\n  </code><code style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\">...</font><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>The way I have written does not seem to work. Apologies for javascript ignorance.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Ian</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dJE7l37_-GEJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2013-08-14T06:59:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: help: composing javascript for conditionalPanel",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It&#39;s not currently possible to use file uploads in conditionalPanel conditions, sorry. You could perhaps create an output on the server to proxy this for you:<div><br></div><div># in server.R</div><div>output$fileUploaded &lt;- reactive({</div>\r\n\r\n<div>  return(!is.null(input$file1))</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>Then your conditionalPanel condition could be &quot;output.fileUploaded&quot;.</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\n\r\nOn Tue, Aug 13, 2013 at 11:27 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ijly...@yahoo.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I would like to make a panel conditional on a file being uploaded.</div><div><br></div><div>One way I think I can do that is to take inspiration from the example shown in <a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#uploads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/%23uploads&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792407464956000&amp;usg=AOvVaw21fGqf3xDbqyYVrlHEYdTB\">http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#uploads</a></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:9px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902)\">\r\n\r\n<code style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;color:inherit;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\">    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># input$file1 will be NULL initially. After the user selects and uploads a </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># file, it will be a data frame with &#39;name&#39;, &#39;size&#39;, &#39;type&#39;, and &#39;datapath&#39; </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># columns. The &#39;datapath&#39; column will contain the local filenames where the </span></span>\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># data can be found.</span></span>\r\n\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inFile</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">file1</span>\r\n\r\n    <span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">if</span></span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">is.null</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inFile</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span>\r\n      <span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">return</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(88,72,246)\">NULL</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span></code></pre>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>I am wondering what is the right way to compose this condition:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:9px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902)\">\r\n\r\n<code style=\"color:inherit;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">conditionalPanel</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span>\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">condition</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;input.file1 != null&quot;</span>,\r\n  </code><code style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\">...</font><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>The way I have written does not seem to work. Apologies for javascript ignorance.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Ian</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div><br></div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
